{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "With only one data point (config_007: scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted → 54.2% acc), the most uncertain and impactful design axis is the RNA encoder, which spans three fundamentally different approaches (learned generative, learned VAE, linear PCA). Config_019 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is a clean single-variable swap from config_007, isolating the RNA encoder effect while holding image encoder, aggregation, and fusion constant. If scvi_n200 performs comparably to scgpt, I can treat learned RNA encoders as interchangeable and focus remaining budget on aggregation/fusion/image-encoder choices; if scgpt is clearly superior, I lock in scgpt and explore other axes. This is the highest-information experiment given 8 remaining slots, as it resolves the largest source of uncertainty before committing to further multimodal tuning."
}

